WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.480
With so many new shows premiering, it's a
pretty competitive field, but these debuting

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.620
series have captivated audiences and critics
alike; so from streaming gems to big network

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.920
efforts, here are the very best TV shows of
2019.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.440
When critics and audiences heard Natasha Lyonne
would be creating her own show for Netflix,

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.200
they paid attention.

00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:24.579
Russian Doll stars Lyonne as Nadia, a woman
stuck in a bizarre time loop where she keeps

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.780
reliving her death on her birthday with absolutely
no explanation or context.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.520
Along the way, she meets Alan, played by Charlie
Barnett, who is stuck in his own terrifying

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.020
time loop.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.320
That leads the two of them to work together
to avoid death, solve their seemingly unsolvable

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.960
problems, and, hopefully, track down Nadia's
missing cat, Oatmeal.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.980
"Hey man, didn't you get the news, we're about
to die."

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.700
"It doesn't matter, I die all the time."

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.440
The series' careful attention to detail, including
small recurring motifs like the ironically

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.289
cheerful Harry Nilsson song that plays every
time Nadia's timeline resets, earned the show

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:05.480
rave reviews, as did Lyonne's performance
in a role she seems born to play.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.800
Along with starring, she also directed the
season finale and created the concept, an

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:14.600
intense involvement that has catapulted her
into praise for her work on both sides of

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.100
the camera.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.300
Though fans are undoubtedly excited for a
second season, Season 1 ended on a rare, perfect

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:20.800
note.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.420
"Thursday!

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:23.420
What a concept!"

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.659
Based on the famously bizarre comic book series
of the same name, Doom Patrol has been called

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.130
the best reason to sign up for the DC Universe
streaming service.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.840
The highly anticipated series premiered in
early 2019 with a 15-episode first season

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.480
focusing on a group of misfit superheroes
trying to save the world from an eerie supernatural

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.400
villain known only as Mr. Nobody.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.580
"Help me out here, I'm inside a donkey or
what?"

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.940
"The question is how do we get outside the
donkey?"

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.320
Doom Patrol racked up an incredible amount
of praise from critics and comic book fans

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.740
alike, and for a show that premiered on a
brand-new platform, based on a relatively

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:05.420
obscure DC property, that says an awful lot
about just how good and refreshingly weird

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:05.920
it is.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.600
Led by Saturday Night Live standout Aidy Bryant
in her first starring role, Hulu's Shrill

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.700
is an adaptation of a book of essays by Lindy
West.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.960
Bryant doesn't directly play West, who serves
as an executive producer on the show, instead

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.700
taking the role of a fictional character named
Annie who aspires to become a journalist while

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.700
figuring out her messy personal life and building
up her self-esteem.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.840
"You're funny!

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.520
You're like Rosie O'Donnell."

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.020
"Ohhhh."

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:37.100
Throughout the first season's six episodes,
Annie stands up to her insensitive boyfriend,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.180
attends a life-changing pool party, and makes
some pretty tough decisions.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.800
Shrill was hailed as a game-changer for plus-sized
women in its portrayal of Annie as a complex,

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:50.480
lovable character who challenges stereotypes
typically seen on television, and praised

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.440
for its willingness to tackle tough issues.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:57.180
With only six episodes under its belt, fans
are dying for more of the series, and they'll

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:57.840
get their wish.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.900
Hulu has already renewed the series for a
second season.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:06.340
An adaptation of the popular comic book series
by Gerard Way, best known as the frontman

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:11.360
for My Chemical Romance, and award-winning
artist Gabriel Bá, The Umbrella Academy premiered

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.960
in February of 2019 to plenty of buzz.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.820
Fans of the original comic books and viewers
excited about a new superhero series with

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:24.030
a killer cast marathoned the ten-episode series
centering on a mysterious school for children

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.720
with supernatural abilities and their lives
as adults in the present day.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.940
Born during a mysterious event when 43 women
around the world gave birth in 1989, despite

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.550
not being pregnant, these children were given
numbers, rather than names, by the Academy's

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.460
headmaster Sir Reginald Hargreeves.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:46.100
After an ill-fated career as teen superheroes,
the dysfunctional family went their separate

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.280
ways, and when they're brought back together
for a funeral, they need to work together

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.060
to prevent an oncoming apocalypse.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.750
Umbrella Academy was a hit for critics and
audiences, and the show was renewed for a

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.360
second season, with the entire cast and creative
team returning for more.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.520
If you loved the 2014 comedy What We Do in
the Shadows, then you'll love FX's television

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.160
version, which premiered in the spring of
2019.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:13.120
With a new cast and a new setting, the series
focuses on three vampires living as roommates

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.569
in New York City's Staten Island, which they
are also trying to conquer for the entire

00:04:17.569 --> 00:04:18.480
race of vampires.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.280
As you might expect, vampiric hijinks ensue.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.480
"You don't seem like someone who would be
capable of killing a vampire."

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.460
"But I did it."

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.160
"Hard to believe."

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.320
"But I did."

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.319
"But maybe from a tougher looking guy, I'd
believe it."

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:33.580
The show was created by Jemaine Clement, who
oversees it alongside Taika Waititi.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:38.740
The pair co-directed the original film, and
the show naturally shares the charming awkwardness

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:39.500
of the movie.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:44.199
It has the same bumbling, deadpan humor that
has characterized much of both Clement and

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:49.240
Waititi's work, from Flight of the Conchords
to Thor: Ragnarok, and it's earned rave reviews.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:53.860
Putting absurd characters in universal situations
has always been a calling card for both of

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:58.160
these creators, and by giving their vampires
new life, they've ended up with another hit

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:58.980
on their hands.

